CamPhish – Awareness
CamPhish is a social engineering tool used to capture images from a target’s device camera through a phishing link.
It tricks the victim into granting camera permission on their browser.
Once permission is allowed, the attacker can capture photos and sometimes location/IP information.
It works by sending a fake webpage or phishing link that looks like a legitimate service.
When the victim opens the link and allows access, the camera activates and captures images silently.

Risks of CamPhish
Unauthorized camera access.
Privacy invasion and spying.
Exposure of personal surroundings or identity.
Possible location tracking using IP information.
Images can be misused or leaked online.
